    "evidence_text": "Delhi Sultanate\n\nEarly Anatolian Animal carpets\n\nEconomy of the Hoysala Empire\n\n The capital of the empire was initially based at Belur, and later transferred to Halebidu.\n\nSociety of the Hoysala Empire\n\nIntabulation\n\nFounding of modern Singapore\n\n It was likely a vassal state of both the Majapahit Empire and the Siamese at different times in the 14th century.\n\nHoysaleswara Temple\n\n During the early 14th century, Halebidu was sacked and looted by Muslim invaders from northern India and the temple fell into a state of ruin and neglect.\n\nLakshminarasimha Temple, Javagal\n\n Halebidu is historically important as the erstwhile capital of the Hoysala empire.\n\n This temple is a protected monument under the Karnataka state division of the Archaeological Survey of India.\n\nHalebidu\n\nHalebeedu (literally \"old capital\") is a town located in Hassan District, Karnataka, India.\n\n It is home to some of the best examples of Hoysala architecture.\n\nHoysala architecture",
